## Boundaries

The estate layer organizes custody and acquisition. It does not duplicate claims or receipts, create graph edges, score subjects, generate conclusions, or approve publication.

A completed slice is not a completed estate. Cross-estate synthesis still requires typed claims, receipts, exact identities, denominators, temporal order, counterweights, and explicit nulls.

