## Purpose

Begins the controlled reconstruction of the EG Addressing protected staff experience under the BeCoreOps Government & Enterprise Design Standard (BGEDS).

## Baseline and dependency

- Base branch: `nli/wo-003-operator-interface-foundation`
- Functional baseline SHA: `515d90dc20583d10a5ac2ff532247087c7e3fd8a`
- This PR is intentionally stacked on PR #12 so it contains only Phase 1 redesign-foundation changes.

## Phase 1 scope

- Establishes BGEDS 1.0 as a cross-project government and enterprise design standard.
- Records the EG Addressing staff-platform findings, reconstruction boundary, target information architecture, workflow model, migration sequence, and evidence gates.
- Adds semantic design tokens without changing current route presentation.
- Adds a non-production `/design-lab` route demonstrating:
  - compact institutional shell;
  - role and territorial context;
  - unified operational summary;
  - queue / record / decision-inspector workbench;
  - restrained status treatment;
  - dense evidence table;
  - personnel-centered staff administration.
- Adds an automated design-foundation guard to the quality suite.

## Preserved systems

No database schema, migrations, API authority, authentication, authorization, lifecycle states, audit rules, publication controls, integrations, citizen capture workflow, or production configuration are changed.

## Production boundary

The design-lab route returns not-found when `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=production`. It contains illustrative data only and is not an official record surface.

## Required validation

- frontend build;
- existing quality and route guards;
- government-design-foundation guard;
- no citizen/public regression;
- exact-head browser review of the design lab on desktop, tablet, and mobile.

## Next milestone after acceptance

Implement the new protected application shell and actionable operator home while preserving current workflows until each replacement is independently validated.

